    "text": "If the magnetic moment and the pole strength of a bar magnet are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3.6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, then its magnetic length is",
